# The allowlist of enabled systemd units, read by ah-noaicheck (see
# ../README.md). One unit name per line ("sshd.service", or a template such
# as "getty@.service", which allows every instance of it); blank lines and
# lines starting with '#' are ignored.
#
# An enabled unit is a link in a *.wants, *.requires or *.upholds folder of
# /etc/systemd/system, /etc/systemd/user or a home's .config/systemd/user.
# Every enabled unit not named here is a hit, so an empty list fails every
# host: the lead fills it from the host's baseline before the first deploy.
# The remote-login unit is left out once remote login is closed, so a release
# that enables it fails its own check.
